00:01:44.972 --> 00:01:50.492
Dividend income screening is how you hunt for payouts backed by regulated or contracted

00:01:50.492 --> 00:01:56.952
cash flow that can compound inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, without immediate

00:01:56.952 --> 00:01:57.632
tax drag.

00:01:58.212 --> 00:02:03.472
You screen first for a yield above 3%, then you check the payout against the latest distributable

00:02:03.472 --> 00:02:08.932
cash flow figure, and you only keep names that use less than 70% of expected cash flow

00:02:08.932 --> 00:02:11.372
so a bad quarter does not force a cut.

00:02:11.372 --> 00:02:16.592
But, last, you compare the multiple with the 5-year average, and you want the stock at or

00:02:16.592 --> 00:02:21.632
below that average, so the yield has room to compound without valuation compression eating

00:02:21.632 --> 00:02:22.532
the total return.

00:02:23.152 --> 00:02:25.912
Think of the yield as the rent attendant promises you.

00:02:26.272 --> 00:02:31.052
The payout ratio is whether their paycheck covers that rent after groceries, and you want

00:02:31.052 --> 00:02:34.752
at least 30% left, so a broken fridge does not bounce the check.

00:02:34.752 --> 00:02:41.072
You pull up a TSX name yielding 3.5%, but the dividend consumes 80% of

00:02:41.072 --> 00:02:45.432
distributable cash flow. Do you buy the income or walk? I walk.

00:02:46.072 --> 00:02:50.572
Coverage is the decision and yield is only the advertisement. Run that screen

00:02:50.572 --> 00:02:54.912
inside your brokerage screener or on TMX Group's investor site using the

00:02:54.912 --> 00:02:58.992
latest quarterly release, pull the third quarter distributable cash flow

00:02:58.992 --> 00:03:03.112
number, and divide the annual dividend by that figure to confirm coverage.

00:03:03.112 --> 00:03:08.552
TMX Group has leaned into data services and subscription models that, according to

00:03:08.552 --> 00:03:14.192
its chief executive, provide recurring revenue, which balances trading volume fees with more

00:03:14.192 --> 00:03:15.112
predictable income.

00:03:15.732 --> 00:03:20.472
The method has delivered steady income in sideways markets, but it can lag when growth

00:03:20.472 --> 00:03:26.692
names rotate higher, as several Canadian financials showed in the 2023 rate hike period when

00:03:26.692 --> 00:03:28.132
they cut or froze dividends.

00:03:28.132 --> 00:03:28.332
Republicans.

00:03:28.792 --> 00:03:30.652
Remember, coverage before yield.

